  "model": "XPERT-PRO",
  "models": [
    "XPERT-PRO",
    "Xpert"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "trinityenergy.co.in",
  "description": "Multifunction meter with RS485 Modbus RTU: voltages, currents, frequency, power factor, powers, demands, DG and EB energies and harmonics",
  "revision": 3,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Trinity Energy Systems, XPERT-PRO Operational Manual, Appendix (Modbus address map)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "XPERT-PRO Operational Manual",
      "note": "section 'Modbus RTU on RS485 Port', Appendix address map and 'Defining multiplication factor'"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Trinity XPERT-PRO. Registers of the Appendix address map (200 to 382). Names are those of the 3P4W column.",
    "All parameters are unsigned long (two registers). The manual gives the addresses in decimal but no example frame; this map keeps the wire addresses of the previous map (address 200 of the table is sent as 199), so it uses address_base 1 with the table's numbers. If a device answers one register off, use address_base 0.",
    "Function 03 reads the registers; at most 254 bytes per request. 4800, 9600 or 19200 baud, 8N1.",
    "Values are multiplied by 100 (the scale here), power factors by 1000, with 1000 added for a leading power factor. DG = diesel generator, EB = electricity board (mains) energy.",
    "Not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 1,
  "x_status": "official",
